The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is

$$
\dfrac{\textrm{d}}{\textrm{d}x}(\arcsch x) = -\dfrac{1}{|x|\sqrt{1+ x^2}}.
$$

Therefore, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}\int \frac{1}{3|x|\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\,\text{d}x=-\frac{1}{3}\int -\frac{1}{|x|\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\,\text{d}x=-\frac{1}{3}\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+C.\end{aligned}
$$

